control"}], "narrative": "Peak before/after contact dissimilarity at the prescribed 5000 half-window is 0.286 (t=42908), well under the 0.6 criterion, and the turnover series is a smooth decaying hump rather than a step. A tighter 3000 bandwidth only reaches 0.324, with isolated single-bin spikes. Data volume is sufficient (~1100 events, 30-34 partners per node) and stable (no bursts; 385/315/396 events across thirds), ruling out volume artefacts. The low edge-level Jaccard (0.154) between adjacent snapshots reflects rotation of which group member is active, not partner replacement: members such as 716 and 1116 both attach to the same persistent ~32-node contact core across the whole window. Verdict: gradual background turnover, no abrupt regime switch."}, "raw_final_response": "**Analysis summary:**\n\n- **Primary metric (step_01):** With the prescribed half-window of 5000, the group's peak before/after contact dissimilarity is **0.2857** at t=42908 \u2014 far below the 0.6 threshold. The series is a smooth hump (0.19 \u2192 0.29 \u2192 decaying to ~0.03), i.e. gradual background turnover, not a step.\n- **Robustness (step_08):** A tighter bandwidth of 3000 raises the peak only to 0.3235; isolated spikes (0.3235 at 47267, 0.3226 at 50344) are single-bin noise, not a sustained old-set\u2192new-set replacement.\n- **Confounder controls:** Volume is flat and burst-free (step_06: 0 bursts; step_10: 385/315/396 events per third), so no activity surge masquerading as a switch. The 0.154 edge-level Jaccard in step_05 is *not* a regime switch: steps 07 and 09 show 1116 and 716 draw on the same ~32-contact core (98, 117, 204, 205, 258, 292, 295, 1045, 1106, 1123, 1155, 1179, 1184, 1247, 1257, 1283, 1294, 1297, 1410, 1460, 1638, 1848, 1950). The apparent edge churn is which *group member* is active, not which *partners* the group talks to \u2014 the contact identity set persists throughout.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_459f9d4b\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [384, 716, 946, 948, 1116, 1121, 1304, 1464, 1572, 1635, 1740, 1955],\n  \"window\": [33806, 63806],\n  \"confidence\": 0.87,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Peak before/after contact dissimilarity at the prescribed 5000 half-window is 0.286 (t=42908), well under the 0.6 criterion, and the turnover series is a smooth decaying hump rather than a step. A tighter 3000 bandwidth only reaches 0.324, with isolated single-bin spikes. Data volume is sufficient (~1100 events, 30-34 partners per node) and stable (no bursts; 385/315/396 events across thirds), ruling out volume artefacts. The low edge-level Jaccard (0.154) between adjacent snapshots reflects rotation of which group member is active, not partner replacement: members such as 716 and 1116 both attach to the same persistent ~32-node contact core across the whole window. Verdict: gradual background turnover, no abrupt regime switch.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 43560, "total_output_tokens": 3393, "total_tokens": 46953, "total_latency_ms": 53873, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "tool_protocol_errors": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}